A real page turner 

@thetimes 

Ok now I’m done x

‘But did you run from Chamonix to Marseille in 45 hours?’ 

Sometimes it’s good to push yourself to a limit you didn’t know you had, and to find yourself somewhere in the middle of France with only your thoughts to cycle through. 

Anyway let me gas up the squaaddd!!!

@suzette_das - the light; a force of competitive nature, never say die, never quit, in it to push herself and us to the max. She set the tone to start the race and never let up. 

@timido_ - the fuel; a go one more mentality that sustained us and gave us an emotional core. Timi gave us her all and had some sandwiches for us to spare.

@runcoachcath - the engine; never meeting a path she couldn’t conquer, Cath was hurtling through the rain, through the dark, each and every turn.

@felix_runs244 - the grit; locked in from the first step, always reminded us of the moment we were in, always thinking about us two steps ahead. I can only aspire to have the love of and respect for the sport that you do.

@geomaros - the heart; a beacon of courage, kindness and calm, he vanished into all the hills and emerged victorious. The man has no quit. I’ll always remember ‘1 toll, 1 trauma’.

@vinganvingan - our Morpheus; plugged into the matrix for 45 hours straight - ‘you think that your body needs sleep to drive for two days?’

@notfriendlyrunningclub - the Zordon to us ‘teenagers with attitude’. Thanks for believing in us!

Anytime you need to run, I’ll answer the call
